  "judgment": {
    "status": "confirmed",
    "reasoning": "All 16 answers agree mathematically with their own captured worked solutions. q-119037: integrating f'=1+6e^{-3x} gives f=x-2e^{-3x}+C. q-119043: integrating y''=6x²-5 twice gives y=x⁴/2-5x²/2+Cx+D. q-50139: integrating y''=-10 twice gives y=-5x²+Cx+D; both arbitrary constants are required. q-119139: y=-2e^{2x}+C has decreasing, concave-down curves with left horizontal asymptotes y=C, matching option 2. q-119142: y=-(x-1)³/4+C has decreasing cubic curves with horizontal inflections at x=1, matching option 0. Each selected graph matches its source graph apart from the source's added constant labels. q-119083: integration gives y=x²+2e^{x/2}+C, and y(0)=2 gives C=0. q-8311: y=-4x+C and y(-1)=4 give C=0. q-79219: squaring and adding gives x²+y²=49. q-106049: option 2 has center (2,1), radius 2, starts at (4,1), and initially moves upward, hence counterclockwise. q-7283: x=t³+t²+C and x(2)=15 give C=3. q-7284: x=t²/8-t³/3+C and x(3)=-7 give C=7/8. q-7111: successive integration with the initial conditions gives v=t-3t²+4 and x=t²/2-t³+4t+2. q-154678 and q-158022: dividing by y² and y respectively gives the source's separated forms, on intervals where y≠0; the original equations also admit y=0. q-154367: integration gives arcsin(y)=x+C, with x+C restricted to (-π/2,π/2) because |y|<1. q-154373: integration gives y^{3/2}=x^{3/2}+C, equivalent to the selected square-root form on the real domain x≥0, y>0. No submitted grades or earlier answers were supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions and independent mathematical verification.",
